target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed: CI must resolve the exact dependency graph rather
# than a fresh resolution that could pull a license-tainted or edition-
# incompatible transitive. The lock also backs the CI freshness gate.
# (Downstream library consumers still resolve their own graph — a committed lock
# does not constrain them.)

# The 4 MiB dfvfs UFS2 Tier-1 oracle image (tests/data/ufs2.raw), its small
# extracted fixtures (ufs2_*.bin) and the minted xattr image (ufs2_xattr.img.gz)
# ARE committed — all well under the ~10 MiB crates.io tarball limit and excluded
# from the published .crate anyway (see forensic/Cargo.toml `exclude`).
#
# Large, re-downloadable corpora live in tests/data/ too — the fleet convention
# (docs/test-corpus-standard.md, and zfs-forensic/.gitignore) is that the data
# sits beside the tests that read it and is kept out of git by EXTENSION, not by
# living somewhere else on the machine. A path outside the repo goes stale, and
# nothing points at it.
#
# The patterns below are deliberately NARROW. zfs-forensic can ignore *.raw and
# *.img wholesale because it commits none; this repo commits ufs2.raw and
# ufs2_xattr.img.gz, so those globs would be actively wrong here.
/tests/data/*.part
/tests/data/*.qcow2
/tests/data/*.qcow2.xz
/tests/data/FreeBSD-*

# OS / editor cruft (belt-and-suspenders alongside a machine-wide core.excludesfile).
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
